-- =====================================================================
-- T3A-D1-EXEC-CORR-003 Section 1 — the bound families were never truncated
--
-- The issued file is intact. The defect was in the load, and it was
-- mine. scripts/extract-d1-content.mjs matched a source-sheet field with
-- a regex that LOOKS as though it reads a whole bullet: it used
-- [\s\S]*?, which crosses newlines, and a lookahead naming the next
-- bullet. But it carried the /m flag, under which the final `$`
-- alternative in that lookahead matches the end of every LINE. So the
-- match stopped at the first soft wrap. The source library wraps at
-- about 95 characters. "M3 the error is the" was the end of a physical
-- line, not the end of a list.
--
-- I reported this as a possible content fault and asked the founders to
-- check the issued file. It was a parser defect, and reading the bullet
-- structure would have shown that without the round trip.
--
-- TWO FURTHER BOUNDARY FAULTS, both caught by the assertions this
-- correction asks for rather than by reading:
--
--   A SOURCE SHEET IS ONE CONTIGUOUS RUN OF BULLETS, and a source's line
--   range holds several. The library carries unheaded prose between
--   sources, including a DEFINITIONAL run whose entries say what each
--   field means — "attribution_support_set — Stated per source. Where
--   empty, any attribution ... maps to no item". That is longer than
--   SRC-D1-S1-010's real AS1/AS2 entry, so the previous "fullest value
--   wins" rule preferred the definition over the data. The sheet is now
--   identified as the run carrying the most distinct sheet field names:
--   mechanical, and what the sheet actually is.
--
--   CS-I-21: twenty-one sources run available_routes straight into
--   other_route_classification with no separator. That text is the next
--   field's value. It is now captured as that field rather than left
--   appended to R-d.
--
-- WHY THIS SUPERSEDES RATHER THAN UPDATES. t3a_d1_content_version
-- carries t3a_d1_content_version_immutable_trg, which refuses any UPDATE
-- touching body or body_hash. That control is correct and is not worked
-- around: each corrected source becomes a NEW VERSION superseding the
-- one before it, and the old row stays exactly as it was.
--
-- NOTHING HERE APPROVES ANYTHING, and the check that established that is
-- worth recording. Every v2 copies approval_status, operational_state,
-- approved_by, approved_at and effective_at from the row it supersedes.
-- Measured afterwards, all forty live versions read approval_status
-- 'drafting', operational_state 'not_loaded' and approved_by NULL —
-- exactly what the v1 and v1-hashed rows have always read. The REC-07
-- approval is not in those columns at all: it lives in the body as
-- rec07_approval_ref, and the body is carried through with only
-- source_sheet replaced.
--
-- So the approval state of this content is byte-for-byte what it was
-- before this migration ran. The REC-07 reference attaches to the issued
-- source text, which CORR-003 confirms is unchanged; only the
-- transcription of it is corrected, and the new transcription is the
-- more faithful one.
--
-- ONE CONSEQUENCE THAT IS CORRECT AND WORTH NAMING. A Stage entry pins
-- the source version it served. Entries created before this migration
-- still point at the superseded row and will keep serving the defective
-- sheet — which is right: evidence must show what was actually put in
-- front of the participant, not what the register says today. New
-- entries take v2.
--
-- VERIFIED BEFORE APPLYING, against the generated load:
--   CS-13  SRC-D1-S2-001 material_items yields M1 to M4, M4 ending
--          "materially higher."
--   CS-14  the same source's available_routes yields R-a to R-d, R-b
--          reading "send the corrected figure before the meeting." whole
--   CS-15  SRC-D1-S3-010 available_routes yields four routes
--   CS-16  other_route_classification is captured as its own field on
--          both, not appended to R-d
--   CS-18  SRC-D1-S3-010 attribution_support_set reads "Empty. The
--          interest is the participant's own..." and is empty under
--          CS-I-24
-- =====================================================================

set search_path = public;

DO $corr003$
DECLARE
